e":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-11T01:56:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T10:08:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.7.2.stable.mono.official.ed1daf0bf.\n\n### Issue description\n\n**Actual:** selected + hovered → normal while held → hover after release.\n\n**Expected:** while previewing deselection under the cursor, the button should retain hover feedback rather than displaying its non-hovered normal style. Activation can still occur on release but this report is about the **intermediate** appearance.\n\n```text\nButton Release: before DRAW_HOVER_PRESSED, held DRAW_NORMAL, released DRAW_HOVER\nButton Press:   before DRAW_HOVER_PRESSED, held DRAW_HOVER,  released DRAW_HOVER\nis_hovered() remained true at each observation.\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add a Button to a new Control scene.\n2. Enable Toggle Mode and set Action Mode to Button Release.\n3. Give the normal, hover, and pressed styles distinct colours.\n4. Run the scene and click the button to select it.\n5. With the cursor still inside, press and hold the mouse button.\n6. The button shows the normal style while held, then the hover style on release.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0